+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static homepage loads the committed `assets/inp.js` bundle. After changing
+instrumentation, run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm build`, and `pnpm test`.
+No runtime CDN or analytics SDK is needed.
+
+## Field INP reporting
+
+Set the `web-vitals-endpoint` meta tag in `index.html` to your deployed collector
+(for example `/analytics/web-vitals`). This repository has no backend: the
+collector must be provisioned separately and accept JSON POSTs. Until configured,
+reports are available only through the `daily-grind:inp` window event. Subscribe
+before the module runs if forwarding reports through an existing analytics SDK:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:inp', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Forward detail to your existing analytics transport.
+});
+```
+
+Delivery uses `sendBeacon`, falling back to `fetch` with `keepalive` when beacon
+is unavailable or refuses the payload. Delivery is best effort; an accepted beacon
+does not guarantee the server received it. Cross-origin collectors need CORS for
+JSON POSTs, and CSP must allow the collector in `connect-src`.
+
+The [web-vitals attribution library](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals)
+calculates the page's INP candidate, handles visibility changes and back/forward
+cache restores, and emits updates when the candidate changes. Reports are **page
+INP candidates, not a log of every interaction**. Upsert by `id` with the latest
+`value` (not the maximum: INP can decrease as the interaction count grows).
+Compute field p75 from one final value per metric ID, including good values;
+filter `rating !== 'good'` when investigating slow visits. INP ratings are good
+at ≤200 ms, need improvement at >200–500 ms, and poor above 500 ms. All timings
+are milliseconds relative to the page's performance time origin.
+
+Each report includes:
+
+- INP value, delta, rating, navigation type, and stable interaction target label.
+- Input delay, event processing duration, and presentation delay.
+- Script, style/layout, paint, and unattributed duration totals where available.
+- The longest overlapping script with its source URL, function, character offset,
+  and INP phase, plus up to ten overlapping scripts ranked by overlap duration.
+- Per-script overlap with each INP phase and forced style/layout duration, plus
+  up to five Long Animation Frame timings and counts of omitted entries.
+
+Long Animation Frame attribution depends on browser support. Missing details
+mean unavailable evidence, not zero work. Frames under 50 ms and scripts under
+5 ms are not attributed by that API, and some cross-origin script details may be
+redacted. Overlapping scripts are diagnostic evidence, not proof of causation.
+Rendering totals are library estimates; `paintDuration` includes off-main-thread
+presentation work and is not an exact GPU trace. Do not add overlapping script
+and layout totals to the three INP phases.
+
+The payload excludes DOM nodes, page text, input values, page URLs, and script
+URL query strings/fragments. Target labels come from `data-inp-target`, falling
+back to the element's tag name. The fixed `page` value identifies this homepage.
+Unsupported browsers and visits without qualifying interactions produce no INP
+report; they must not be recorded as zero-duration visits.
